 {
  "name": "F1 the slots calls are not part of the Wave21 fence",
  "file": "compiler/src/formats.cpp",
  "old": "                   n.rfind(\"slots.\",0)==0;                // CP-01/CP-04: owned slots",
  "new": "                   false;                // CP-01/CP-04: owned slots",
  "tests": [
   "tests/cp01_owned_slots.py",
   "RepresentationTests"
  ],
  "equivalent": "Every slots.* call in a bundle presupposes a slots.alloc<T> of a nominal resource T in the same bundle; the only source of a Resource<T> value is resource.seal, which is already in the Wave21/OMC21 fence (hardwareIntrinsicName), so a program with slots.* and without seal cannot exist and the slots entry never decides the label. It is kept as defence in depth."
 },
